# Security, isolation and caching headers (Cloudflare Pages format; Netlify reads it too).
# The Content-Security-Policy itself is set per page in Layout.astro.
#
# Cross-origin isolation (COOP same-origin + COEP require-corp) makes
# crossOriginIsolated true, which unlocks SharedArrayBuffer and WebAssembly
# threads for the FFmpeg, AI and PDF engines. Every resource the site loads is
# same-origin; the only third-party script (Google Analytics, optional) loads in
# CORS mode. Workers and WASM files are covered by the same /* rule.
# GitHub Pages ignores this file: previews there are not isolated, and the
# media engine falls back to its single-thread build.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/local-engine/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/models/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
